- Form the post-normalization mantissa before classifying special encodings. For BASE_WIDTH > 1,
  a shifted carry is not generally the mantissa MSB.
- EXPONENT_MAX_VALUE is the all-ones EXPONENT_WIDTH field, zero-extended to the intermediate width.
- Any positive exponent above that value overflows, regardless of the mantissa MSB.
- At the maximum exponent, mantissa MSB=1 remains the documented reserved NaN/Inf representation.
- Preserve the existing encoding rule at exponent zero: mantissa MSB=0 is unsupported subnormal and flushes to zero.
- Negative exponents also flush to zero. On overflow clamp the exponent to its maximum and set the reserved mantissa MSB.
